From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: gen1: accept P010 encoder input for HEVC Main 10

The encoder only takes NV12 and QC08C input, so it cannot produce HEVC
Main 10. A client can still select the Main 10 profile with NV12 input:
the gen1 firmware then runs the session as 10-bit anyway (for 8-bit
input it warns that the encoded data will be random), while the driver
sized the internal buffers for 8 bits.

Offer P010 as encoder input on HFI gen1 cores with four VPP pipes
(SM8250, SC8280XP) when the coded format is HEVC. The gen1 firmware can
refuse 10-bit encoding on smaller cores at the first frame, and gen2 has
no 10-bit input setup yet, so neither offers it. For P010:

- bytesperline is ALIGN(width * 2, 256) and the buffer size follows the
  P010 layout (Y scanlines aligned to 32, UV to 16), the layout the
  decoder already outputs and gralloc allocates;
- the width is limited to 4096 (TRY_FMT and S_FMT clamp it,
  ENUM_FRAMESIZES reports it for P010 and ENUM_FRAMEINTERVALS refuses
  wider P010 frames), the stride limit of 8192 bytes the plane
  constraints below declare;
- UNCOMPRESSED_FORMAT_SELECT carries HFI_COLOR_FORMAT_P010 and
  UNCOMPRESSED_PLANE_ACTUAL_INFO the byte stride;
- UNCOMPRESSED_PLANE_ACTUAL_CONSTRAINTS_INFO is sent for the input
  (stride multiple 256, scanlines 32/16, alignment 256), as downstream
  msm_vidc does for P010; the packetizer now passes encoder input
  constraints through and keeps the fixed decoder OUTPUT2 values;
- SCRATCH_1 and SCRATCH_2 are sized for 10 bits. The gen1 encoder has
  no LINE or VPSS buffers;
- the bitstream (CAPTURE) buffers of HEVC are a quarter larger, as
  downstream msm_vidc sizes them for 10 bits. Their size was computed
  only when the coded format or the frame size was set, while the
  stateful encoder interface has the client set the coded format
  first, so S_FMT on OUTPUT now updates the CAPTURE size when the input
  bit depth changes.

The input formats depend on the coded format, so S_FMT on CAPTURE with a
coded format that does not take the current input format (H.264 after
HEVC with P010) now sets the input format back to NV12 at the same size,
as the stateful encoder interface allows, instead of leaving a format
that ENUM_FMT no longer lists and STREAMON refuses. With OUTPUT buffers
allocated it fails with -EBUSY instead. S_FMT on CAPTURE now also sets
the coded format before it computes the bitstream size.

At STREAMON on gen1, require 10-bit input exactly for HEVC Main 10 and
refuse both mismatches with -EINVAL and a log line. Main 10 with NV12
input could be set before and is refused now; no other combination
changes.

Checked on SC8280XP (wrapper version 0x60100608, four pipes): P010 input
is coded into Main 10 streams that keep the 10-bit precision, with the
chroma order and levels intact, from 1920x1080 to 4096x2176 (at a 60 fps
operating rate), in VBR and CBR, next to an 8-bit encode and after a
client was killed mid-stream; both mismatches are refused at STREAMON.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
